280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Random Search: A type of suspicionless search. These searches are not conducted out of individual suspicion but as a preventive measure since schools have the legal obligation to protect everyone there. The legality of a random search depends on whether the school has a proven problem, compelling interest, or special need that justifies the use of a search without suspicion and whether the random search has to do with the duty to protect its students and staff. A random search needs a special-needs exception. Based on the proven problem the school has, the school may choose a group of students, such as a grade or a team, to conduct a random search on, but the idea of a random search is that within the group that is chosen to have a random search, those who are searched are chosen completely at random. Consequences that arise after a random search also play a part in whether it was constitutional, such as treatment, support, criminal consequences, law enforcement, or punishments.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
