390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (Another personal search is the search of a student. The search generally must be justified by reasonable grounds at its beginning and must be reasonably related in scope to the circumstances that justified it. Firstly, a search of a student can include looking through pockets, asking a student to empty their pockets, searching clothing or outerwear, a pat-down, or a similar physical search. For a regular individualized search by a public-school official, they usually need reasonable grounds to believe that the search will uncover evidence of a violation of a school rule or the law. The suspicion should be connected to the student and the thing being sought.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
